Install pip (Python’s package manager):

pip3 --version
pip 22.0.2 from /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip (python 3.10)
If not, install it:
sudo apt install python3-pip -y


Create the virtual enviornment:

step1 : Install the venv package
Run this command:
sudo apt install python3.10-venv -y

Step 2: Recreate your virtual environment
Now that venv is installed, recreate your environment:
python3 -m venv venv


Step 3: Activate the environment
source venv/bin/activate

Once activated, your terminal prompt will change to something like:
(venv) bharti@MLLLAPH01647:~/Documents/ai_todo_app$


Step 2: Install Core Libraries

These are the essential libraries for handling data, basic AI, and logic:

pip install numpy pandas scikit-learn nltk

NumPy → Handles numbers and arrays
Pandas → Helps store and process task lists easily
Scikit-learn → Machine learning toolkit (for priorities, recommendations, etc.)
NLTK → Natural language tools (for understanding text like “remind me to call mom”)